You two have been playing Moria too much.  There are certain cases,
particularly on the castle level, where some spell that is pretty much
useless anywhere else, such as levitation or opening, becomes
absolutely essential.  This is where spell books can really come in
handy.

Not to mention the fact that there is a reasonably effective way of
creating new spell books if you have the proper props with which to do
it.  Of course, you could do something similar to get wands or rings,
but only a masochist would reverse-genocide minotaurs.

